We only need each todo's status and parent, so we index those by
id rather than deserializing full todo items.
The error handling matches the real reader's granularity: on any
problem with [[todos.json]], [[load_todos_raw]] discards the whole
file and returns no todos, whereupon normalization drops every
stack id.
Empty maps achieve the same.

<<read the todo statuses>>=
status_by_id = {}
parent_by_id = {}
try:
    with open(directory / TODO_FILE) as todo_file:
        data = json.load(todo_file)
    for item in data.get("todos", []):
        todo_id = int(item["id"])
        status_by_id[todo_id] = item.get("status", "pending")
        parent = item.get("parent_id")
        parent_by_id[todo_id] = (
            None if parent is None else int(parent)
        )
except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, TypeError):
    status_by_id = {}
    parent_by_id = {}
